---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import katex from 'katex';
import 'katex/dist/katex.min.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const typeset = (latex: string) =>
  katex.renderToString(latex, {
    output: 'htmlAndMathml',
    throwOnError: true,
  });

const directionEquation = typeset(
  String.raw`\mathit{Direction}_{t} = \beta_{0}\mathit{leader}_{t} + \beta_{1}X_{t} + u_{t}`,
);
const betaZero = typeset(String.raw`\beta_{0}`);
---

<Base
  title="What about virtue? | Elisa Diop-Weyer"
  description="What about virtue?, by emdw."
>
  <article class="essay-page">
    <a class="back-link" href={`${base}/musings/`}>← Selected Outputs</a>

    <header>
      <h1>What about virtue?</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="essay-body">
      <p>I shopped a class on medical ethics and halfway through the first lecture the girl with whom I was sitting scribbled on her notebook: “What about virtue?” -- I borrow this for this title.</p>

      <p>Thinking about deontology today re tech CEOs:</p>

      <ol class="main-list">
        <li>LLMs and ontology expand the dystopia -- utopia option horizon dramatically;</li>
        <li>The expansion seems symmetrical on both normative tails, which I think makes it difficult for a consequentialist to make a normative statement about these technologies. There is too much stochasticity involved to predict what the consequence of a given technological development will be;</li>
        <li>A deontologist making a normative statement about the virtue of a CEO can make a normative statement using information that exists (published things a CEO has said);</li>
        <li>So it is very difficult to be a consequentialist in this epistemic environment and it is tempting to default to deontology;</li>
        <li>
          Which is why, on my view, there is much public angst re the personal lives and motivations of an Amodei, Altman, Karp, Thiel, Musk<sup id="fnref-1"><a href="#fn-1" aria-label="Footnote 1">1</a></sup> etc.; because we were all forced into deontology to make judgements about the technologies they spearhead; we must trust their judgement given the breadth of the option horizon.

          <ol class="sub-list" type="a">
            <li>In general, if you model <span class="math" set:html={directionEquation}></span>, <span class="math" set:html={betaZero}></span> for a tech company &gt; <span class="math" set:html={betaZero}></span> for the median government or NGO in 2026, by nature (virtue?) of regulation, bureaucracy etc. For better and for worse.</li>
          </ol>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <section class="footnotes" aria-label="Footnotes">
        <ol>
          <li id="fn-1">I list him not because I think X.ai is a frontier lab (I don’t); I’m mostly thinking about Starlink and Ukraine. <a class="footnote-back" href="#fnref-1" aria-label="Back to footnote reference">↩</a></li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="signature">-- emdw 20261019</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .essay-page {
    width: min(100%, 48rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back-link:hover,
  .back-link:focus-visible {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  h1 {
    font-style: italic;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .essay-body {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .essay-body > p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .main-list,
  .sub-list {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 2.25rem;
  }

  .main-list > li {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 0.2rem;
  }

  .main-list > li::marker {
    content: "(" counter(list-item) ")  ";
  }

  .sub-list {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .sub-list > li {
    padding-left: 0.2rem;
  }

  .sub-list > li::marker {
    content: counter(list-item, lower-alpha) ".  ";
  }

  .math {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .math :global(.katex) {
    font-size: 1em;
  }

  sup {
    line-height: 0;
  }

  sup a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .footnotes {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.14);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .footnotes ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .footnote-back {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .signature {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    text-align: right;
  }
</style>
